@startuml
' System-level context diagram for section 2.1.2.
' Authored in Slice 1. Renders through scripts/render-diagrams.sh.
!include style.puml
title Context diagram: the system and its environment

left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

actor "Store\nmanager" as SM
actor "DC\nmanager" as DM
node "External\nPOS system\n(one per store)" as POS #dae8fc
node "External\nsupplier/ERP\nsystem" as ERP #dae8fc

rectangle "**Supermarket Inventory Tracking System**" as SYS {
  rectangle "Store\n(3 today, up to 10)" as ST #d5e8d4
  rectangle "Distribution center" as DCB #fff2cc
}

POS --> ST : sales records
SM --> ST : inventory queries
ST --> DCB : inventory events\n[secure channel]
DCB --> ERP : purchase and\nshipping orders
ERP --> DCB : goods-receipt\nconfirmations
DM --> DCB : queries, reports,\nshipping orders

legend bottom
  The outer box is our system boundary. Green is the store side; yellow is the
  distribution center. Blue nodes are external systems; stick figures are human
  roles. Arrows show the information that crosses each connection.
endlegend
@enduml
